/specs/

# `tests/` USED TO BE IGNORED HERE, and it was version 1's test output. In
# version 2 it is the source of three of the five test tiers — integration,
# component and security — and the rule quietly kept every one of them out of
# the repository. On a fresh clone those tiers matched no files at all, so CI
# ran a fraction of what the README claimed and every regression test written
# for the editor stayed on one laptop.
#
# `/specs/` keeps its leading slash for the same class of reason: it means
# version 1's leftover directory at the root, not any `specs` folder that a
# package might grow.

# Fonts are vendored in assets/fonts and COPIED into the app at build
# time. One source of truth; the copy is build output.
apps/web/public/fonts/

# === Generated previews ===
design-preview.html
shots/
.shots/

# === Portable packages are build output, not source ===
*.vuchant
*.smdoc

# === Claude Code local config ===
# CLAUDE.md is COMMITTED: it is the map a contributor or agent needs on clone.
# Only machine-local settings are ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# === OS / editor ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Declaration output that lands next to a source file. It should never be
# there — it means a project emitted with the wrong rootDir — but ignoring it
# stops one bad invocation committing 40 generated files, which happened.
src/**/*.d.ts
src/**/*.d.ts.map
dist-types/
.work/

# Screenshots and measurements the tools write for us to look at.
/artifacts/

# The Lexical spike bundles itself; the bundle and its font are build products.
/tools/spike-lexical/spike.js
/tools/spike-lexical/*.woff2
